=== SURVEY ===
Web source of truth: web/src/components/motion/RouteTransition.tsx (92 lines, read end-to-end) +
  web/src/hooks/useMotionPreference.ts.
  Data: useLocation() (current pathname) + useMotionPreference(120) ({ reduce, durationMs }).
  Behaviour: cross-fades route content on `pathname` change — 120ms ease-out fade + 4px y-lift
    (initial y:4, exit y:-4); `mode="wait"`; `initial={false}` (no entry animation on cold load);
    re-keyed by `location.pathname` ONLY (query/hash never re-fade); honours prefers-reduced-motion
    (fade collapses to 0); DEFAULT_SKIP_PATTERNS suppress list↔detail drill-in/out on EITHER side:
      /drives/:id, /drives/:id/replay, /charging/:id, /vehicles/:id, /vehicles/:id/access, /trips/:id.
  i18n: NONE — the component is an anonymous motion wrapper (no t() calls, renders no prose).
  Charts/maps/shared-components used by the source: NONE (per the prompt manifest).

=== REASONING ===
Architecture (self-contained 7-file bundle, the proven sibling convention; NO `import Shared` so the
  surface compiles + unit-tests without the KMP framework):
  (1) RouteTransition.Projection.swift — PURE Foundation core: `RoutePathPattern` (a faithful port of
      react-router v6 `matchPath({ path, end:true }, pathname)` for static + `:param` syntax —
      case-insensitive, `:param` = one non-empty segment, full-path consumption, trailing-slash
      tolerant); `matchesAnySkip`; `decide(...)` reproducing `effectiveDurationMs = reduce ||
      skipForList ? 0 : durationMs` plus the `initial={false}` cold-load no-entry rule (precedence
      reduce > skip > first-render > animated); `resolve(...)` + `normalizedPath(...)` for the phase.
  (2) RouteTransition.Model.swift — P1/S10 i18n facade, value types, the live-state Connection axis,
      the P1/S11 telemetry seam + OSLog default, the input snapshot, the resolved phase, the P1/S8
      `RouteTransitionSource` seam, the `@MainActor @Observable RouteTransitionModel` (prev/current
      path + first-render tracking → re-keys ONLY on real pathname change, `view.opened` once, a
      one-shot stale auto-refresh that re-arms on live), and `InMemoryRouteTransitionSource`.
  (3) RouteTransition.Views.swift — the cross-fade content host (`.id(pathname)` + asymmetric
      opacity/offset transition gated by the decision, `nil` animation when suppressed — the native
      peer of AnimatePresence/motion.div), plus the leaf chrome (loading indicator, empty state,
      retryable error) and the live/stale/offline freshness chip, all on P1/S9 tokens.
  (4) RouteTransition.swift — the generic surface `RouteTransition<Content>`: binds the model,
      renders EVERY phase, reads reduced-motion from the SwiftUI environment (native peer of
      `useMotionPreference`/prefers-reduced-motion), overlays the freshness chip, starts/stops.
  (5) RouteTransition.Previews.swift — one #Preview per state (content / list-detail-instant /
      loading / empty / error / stale / offline). (Reduced motion is exercised via Xcode's preview
      canvas toggle — the iOS 26.5 SDK makes `accessibilityReduceMotion` a read-only EnvironmentKey,
      so a `.environment(\.…, true)` override does not compile; that was caught + removed.)
  (6) RouteTransition.Tests.swift — 37 unit tests (adapter + per-state + a11y).
  (7) RouteTransition.strings — the "RouteTransition" i18n table (10 keys, all leaf chrome since the
      web wrapper is anonymous — no English literals live in the Swift sources).
Leaf-contract states (loading/empty/error/stale/offline) are the sanctioned P4 additions over the
  anonymous web wrapper (documented in-source), exactly as the AiUsageCard sibling adds error/stale/
  offline over its web source. Every state renders real UI — never a blank box.
Rejected: (a) depending on the atomic `TSRouteTransition` in Sources/Components/Motion (it is the
  P4 component-library bundle's concern — explicitly OUT OF SCOPE here); (b) `import Shared` /
  StateHolderModel (would not compile without the KMP framework and is composition-root work);
  (c) editing project.yml/.swiftlint.yml to register the dir (outside allowed files — see boundary).

